  "body": "## Summary\n- **Log → Meal** opens a **Saved meals** list (\"No saved meals yet.\" when empty), a **+ New saved meal** button, and **Log a meal without saving it**.\n- **Saved meals** have their own screen for name, calories and protein per portion, with Save/Cancel, an edit button on each, and delete. Saving one logs nothing.\n- **Logging**: tap a saved meal, then set portion, date, time and notes, then **Log meal**. Numbers can be changed for that one meal; the screen says the saved meal keeps its numbers. Logging never creates or changes a saved meal.\n- **Data**: `meal-template` (shared saved meal, one set of numbers per portion) and `meal-entry` (numbers stored as eaten, so changing or deleting a saved meal never rewrites past days). No migration.\n- **Overview**: a Meals column with one daily-total node per day, a Show/Hide toggle, and a hover panel. Clicking opens the meal day with per-meal Edit and + Add meal.\n\n## Verification\n- Backend `npm test` 11 pass; frontend `npm test` 10 pass, `eslint .` clean, `vite build` ok.\n- Dev server against live DB, nothing written: `/api/meals` and `/api/meal-templates` return `[]`, invalid POST rejected with 400. Walked every meal screen (list, new saved meal, one-off, back navigation) on the real empty data; the tap-a-saved-meal and edit-saved-meal paths were checked with one in-page fake saved meal and writes blocked.",
